course: dictionary
lesson: 2145
title: One word, many meanings: copper
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Copper can be a metal, a colour, a coin, or a police officer. The words around it tell you which meaning is right. «Copper wire» is the metal. «Copper coins» are the small brown coins.
explain: Ask yourself what the sentence is about. «Metals pass heat along very well, and electricity too, which is why wires are copper inside their plastic coat.» Heat and electricity are about science, so copper is the metal. Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: Be careful with informal words. In Britain, a copper is a police officer, and that is a different meaning again. You can only know which meaning is right by reading the whole sentence and thinking about its topic.
fact: Copper is a reddish-brown metal.
fact: Copper conducts electricity and heat very well, so it is used for electric wires.
fact: Copper is also a reddish-brown colour.
fact: In Britain, coppers can mean small brown coins, and a copper is an informal word for a police officer.
fact: Bronze is an alloy, a mixture of copper and tin.
exercise: «Metals pass heat along very well, and electricity too, which is why wires are copper inside their plastic coat.» What does copper mean here? | A brown paint | A police officer | *A reddish-brown metal | A small brown coin
exercise: Sam found three coppers down the back of the sofa. What are coppers here? | *Small brown coins | Electric wires | Police officers | Metal pipes
exercise: «Bronze is an alloy of copper and tin; it is harder than either metal.» What is bronze made from? | Tin and plastic | *Copper and tin | Iron and gold | Copper and salt
test: Many countries are switching off old «copper phone lines». What are these lines made of? | Glass only | *Wire made from copper metal | Plastic | Wood
test: In Britain, what does the informal word copper mean? | *A police officer | A metal pipe | A kind of bronze | A small brown coin
exam: Which informal British word means a police officer? | wire | bronze | coin | *copper
